cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Dograh Experiments
message: >-
  If you use these experiments, their data or their results, please cite
  the repository and the individual experiment you used.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: Dograh
    website: https://dograh.com
repository-code: https://github.com/RuchiketJadhav/experiments
url: https://dograh.com/hub/experiments
abstract: >-
  Voice AI experiments from the Dograh team, published with the data,
  the generator and the results together so every number can be checked.
  Each experiment ships a free verification step that recomputes the
  published figures from the published data.
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: https://github.com/RuchiketJadhav/experiments/blob/main/LICENSE
date-released: "2026-09-30"
keywords:
  - voice-ai
  - text-to-speech
  - speech-recognition
  - benchmark
  - text-normalization
  - reproducibility
references:
  - type: data
    title: >-
      TTS verbalization benchmark: do open text-to-speech models say dates,
      prices and phone numbers correctly?
    authors:
      - name: Dograh
    url: https://dograh.com/hub/experiments/tts-verbalization-benchmark
    repository-code: https://github.com/RuchiketJadhav/experiments/tree/main/benchmarks/tts-verbalization
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    date-released: "2026-09-30"
    abstract: >-
      Seven open text-to-speech models over 1,080 generated sentences in 27
      categories, scored by two independent speech recognizers. Data,
      generator and results published together.
